## 9. Operator Installation

Install via OLM using Namespace → OperatorGroup → Subscription. All operators are sourced from the mirrored catalog (`cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22`).

**Generic pattern** (example: Compliance Operator):
```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: openshift-compliance
---
apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1
kind: OperatorGroup
metadata:
  name: compliance-operator
  namespace: openshift-compliance
spec:
  targetNamespaces: [openshift-compliance]
---
apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1alpha1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: compliance-operator
  namespace: openshift-compliance
spec:
  channel: stable
  name: compliance-operator
  source: cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22      # mirrored CatalogSource name
  sourceNamespace: openshift-marketplace
  installPlanApproval: Manual                # production: review upgrades
```
Find channel/source: `oc get packagemanifest compliance-operator -o jsonpath='{.status.defaultChannel}'`.
Approve InstallPlans: `oc get installplan -n <ns>` → `oc patch installplan <name> -n <ns> --type merge -p '{"spec":{"approved":true}}'`.

