### 9.2 Logging (Loki + Vector) minimum config

```yaml
# NooBaa bucket for Loki
apiVersion: objectbucket.io/v1alpha1
kind: ObjectBucketClaim
metadata: {name: loki-bucket, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec:
  generateBucketName: loki
  storageClassName: openshift-storage.noobaa.io
```
Create secret `logging-loki-s3` from the OBC's ConfigMap/Secret (`BUCKET_NAME`, `BUCKET_HOST`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`), then:
```yaml
apiVersion: loki.grafana.com/v1
kind: LokiStack
metadata: {name: logging-loki, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec:
  size: 1x.small               # 1x.medium for larger clusters
  storage:
    schemas: [{version: v13, effectiveDate: "2024-10-01"}]
    secret: {name: logging-loki-s3, type: s3}
  storageClassName: ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd
  tenants: {mode: openshift-logging}
  template:
    ingester: {nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""}, tolerations: [{key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule},{key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}]}
    # repeat nodeSelector/tolerations for querier, queryFrontend, distributor, compactor, gateway, indexGateway, ruler
---
apiVersion: observability.openshift.io/v1
kind: ClusterLogForwarder
metadata: {name: collector, namespace: openshift-logging}
spec:
  serviceAccount: {name: collector}
  outputs:
    - name: default-lokistack
      type: lokiStack
      lokiStack: {target: {name: logging-loki, namespace: openshift-logging}, authentication: {token: {from: serviceAccount}}}
      tls: {ca: {key: service-ca.crt, configMapName: openshift-service-ca.crt}}
  pipelines:
    - name: all-logs
      inputRefs: [application, infrastructure, audit]
      outputRefs: [default-lokistack]
```
Grant the `collector` SA: `collect-application-logs`, `collect-infrastructure-logs`, `collect-audit-logs` cluster roles.

