## 11. Backup, Updates and DR

### 11.1 etcd backup (CronJob on a control-plane node)

```yaml
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata: {name: etcd-backup, namespace: openshift-etcd}
spec:
  schedule: "0 */6 * * *"
  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid
  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/master: ""}
          tolerations: [{key: node-role.kubernetes.io/master, effect: NoSchedule}]
          hostNetwork: true
          hostPID: true
          serviceAccountName: etcd-backup
          restartPolicy: Never
          containers:
            - name: backup
              image: registry.example.com:8443/openshift4/ose-tools-rhel9:latest
              securityContext: {privileged: true}
              command: ["/bin/bash","-c"]
              args:
                - chroot /host /usr/local/bin/cluster-backup.sh /home/core/backup/$(date +%F-%H%M) &&
                  find /host/home/core/backup -mtime +7 -delete
              volumeMounts: [{name: host, mountPath: /host}]
          volumes: [{name: host, hostPath: {path: /}}]
```
Grant the SA `privileged` SCC. **Sync backups off-node** (rsync/NFS/S3) and **test a restore** on a staging cluster.

### 11.2 Application backup — OADP

```yaml
apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: DataProtectionApplication
metadata: {name: dpa, namespace: openshift-adp}
spec:
  configuration:
    velero: {defaultPlugins: [openshift, aws, csi]}
    nodeAgent: {enable: true, uploaderType: kopia}
  backupLocations:
    - velero:
        provider: aws
        default: true
        objectStorage: {bucket: oadp-backups, prefix: ocp-prod}
        config: {region: noobaa, s3ForcePathStyle: "true", s3Url: https://s3.openshift-storage.svc}
        credential: {name: cloud-credentials, key: cloud}
```
Schedule: `velero schedule create daily --schedule="0 2 * * *" --include-namespaces '*' --ttl 720h`.

### 11.3 Cluster updates (disconnected)

1. Mirror the target release with oc-mirror (update `maxVersion` in ImageSetConfiguration) and push to the registry.
2. Apply new `signature-configmap.yaml` and updated IDMS.
3. OSUS graph refreshes automatically; `oc adm upgrade` lists the target.
4. Pre-checks: `oc get co`, `oc get mcp`, `oc adm upgrade`, no `PodDisruptionBudget` blocking drains, etcd backup taken.
5. Pause worker MCPs for staged rollout (EUS-to-EUS): `oc patch mcp worker -p '{"spec":{"paused":true}}' --type merge`.
6. `oc adm upgrade --to=4.22.17` (control plane first), unpause pools, monitor `oc get mcp -w`.
7. Always test the exact path in a non-prod cluster first.

### 11.4 DR runbook (document and rehearse)

- Control-plane node replacement (`oc adm cordon/drain`, re-boot with agent ISO is **not** supported for day-2 — use BMH/MachineSet or the `oc adm node-image create` flow for adding nodes).
- Full etcd restore: `cluster-restore.sh` procedure.
- Certificate expiry recovery (CSR approval after prolonged shutdown).
- Loss of mirror registry: Quay backup (`/opt/quay/storage`, postgres dump).

